[acct2-main] SDK 0211, 2026-11-14 (owner 15:31: "We want a safe environment when playing online"; claimed on the board
at 18:16, a free number beside 0209/0210; dev/agents/acct2-main/MP-SAFETY.md gap 1 a).
What it does: with net_lan_only on (the default), system link also exchanges packets with the addresses named in
net_broadcast_peers, not only with local network addresses. A friend over a VPN whose range isn't private (Tailscale's
100.64.0.0/10, for example) or on another subnet can then play without turning net_lan_only off, which lets every
internet address in. Only an address the local-network rule refused is looked up, so nothing changes on a local
network; the list is parsed again only when the setting's text changes (0209's parser, moved up unchanged, which the
broadcast still uses). The block warning says the address can be named there. 100.64.0.0/10 as a whole stays out on
purpose: an internet provider's carrier-grade NAT shares it with its other customers. No new setting; the help texts
of net_lan_only and net_broadcast_peers say so.
To test: system link with net_lan_only on and the other PC's non-local address named in net_broadcast_peers (it joins);
the same without naming it (blocked, logged once with the new hint). Checked so far: git apply --check on REA's
build tree, applied before 0315 (the later patch to this file) and 0315 after it, a syntax compile with the SDK
build's flags (no new warning).

